<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Roadmap Planning Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Product roadmaps can become ineffective when teams treat them as fixed
                    delivery schedules rather than strategic planning tools. Changing
                    priorities, competing stakeholder requests, limited resources, and
                    unclear objectives can make roadmap management difficult.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Too Many Priorities:</b> Focus the roadmap on a manageable number of high-value strategic initiatives.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Unclear Objectives:</b> Connect every major roadmap initiative with a clear customer or business outcome.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Stakeholder Conflicts:</b> Use transparent prioritization criteria and evidence to create alignment between teams.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Unrealistic Timelines:</b> Build delivery expectations around actual capacity, dependencies, technical complexity, and resources.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Constant Changes:</b> Review proposed changes based on customer impact, business value, urgency, and strategic importance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Lack of Customer Input:</b> Use research, feedback, analytics, and market information to validate roadmap priorities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Poor Communication:</b> Share roadmap direction clearly with internal teams and appropriate external stakeholders.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant roadmap challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

