                    achievable timeframes. Effective timelines should provide useful
                    visibility while allowing enough flexibility to handle uncertainty
                    and changes during product development.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Define major roadmap milestones and expected delivery stages.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Consider team capacity, technical complexity, and development dependencies.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Coordinate roadmap initiatives with release and sprint planning.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Communicate timelines as planning targets rather than unnecessary rigid commitments.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Update timelines when new information materially affects delivery expectations.</p>
