<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>How to Measure Product Roadmap Planning Effectiveness</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Measuring roadmap effectiveness helps organizations determine whether
                    planned initiatives are delivering the expected customer and business
                    value. Roadmap metrics should focus on outcomes rather than simply
                    measuring the number of features delivered.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Roadmap Goal Achievement:</b> Measure progress toward the strategic objectives connected to roadmap initiatives.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Delivery Predictability:</b> Compare planned initiatives and timelines with actual delivery performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Customer Impact:</b> Evaluate whether delivered initiatives solve meaningful customer problems.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Feature Adoption:</b> Track how effectively roadmap investments are adopted and used by customers.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Business Outcomes:</b> Monitor revenue, growth, retention, conversion, efficiency, or other expected results.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Stakeholder Alignment:</b> Evaluate whether teams have a shared understanding of product priorities and direction.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant analytics image here when available. *@
